<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm6c-taiyuan-2026-11-21 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 6C / Unknown Payload (Taiyuan LC-9A) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
thrust SL/vac interpolated on ambient pressure, mdot from Isp, staging/fairing/coast events; vertical rise to 32.5 s (rule: config guidance),
pitch kick 0.041 deg over 10 s, gravity turn, linear-tangent upper-stage steering tan(theta)=0.2583-0.002789*(t-t_ign), solved by optimizer.
Vehicle config: Long March 6C (2x YF-100 / YF-115, no boosters) (sim/vehicles/lm6c.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
LM-6C stage data: GLOW 217 t, diameters, 2x YF-100 and 1x YF-115 from Wikipedia &#x27;Long March 6C&#x27;. Sea-level thrust 2376 kN is that infobox. Vacuum thrust is derived with the YF-100 1340/1200 kN pair from Wikipedia &#x27;Long March 8&#x27;. Isp 335 s and 341.5 s are from Wikipedia &#x27;Long March 6&#x27; (the LM-6C infobox mis-labels those second figures as kN).
Propellant and dry masses are not published for LM-6C. S2 propellant 15 t is borrowed from the Long March 6 YF-115 stage. S2 dry 2 t, fairing 1.2 t, payload 1 t and the S1 0.910 propellant fraction are ASSUMPTIONS chosen so the pieces sum to the 217 t GLOW. Energy-cutoff mode: no ignition/cutoff sequence is published.
ILLUSTRATIVE. PRE-FLIGHT. Long March 6C, unknown payload, Taiyuan Launch Complex 9A. LL2 id 13270554-4bdb-42ae-916f-1bb54492204f, status Go, NET 2026-11-21T03:50:00Z (Fri 20 Nov 7:50 p.m. PST), window 03:46-04:15Z, orbit Unknown (net precision Hour). Wikipedia&#x27;s launch table lists this row as Y3, payload unknown, planned.
No Chinese NOTAM or navigation-warning polygon for this window was found, so the azimuth is an ASSUMPTION: 189.52 deg, the non-rotating southbound azimuth for a 97.40 deg / 500 km SSO from this pad. Prior LM-6C Taiyuan flights were SSO.
Vehicle is vehicles/lm6c.json. Energy-cutoff (no published timeline). Target 500 km circular is ASSUMED. Payload 1000 kg is ASSUMED. No deploy time is published.
Target (see launch config): insertion 500 km, apoapsis 500 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 189.52 deg; payload 1000 kg.
Pad: 38.858300N 111.580200E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-21T03:50:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: deploy time unpublished (No payload-deploy time is published. LL2 gives the mission as Unknown Payload with no separation time.). From insertion T+485.5 s the stage is propagated for TWO revolutions (osculating period 95.07 min) on the inferred insertion orbit (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model); rows tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF end T+11894 s: inferred insertion orbit, +2 revs (deploy time unpublished): alt 500.0 km, osculating 495.6 x 548.5 km, i 96.649 deg.
POST-CUTOFF note: Upper-stage residual venting after cutoff is not modelled.</description>
